1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,733
Thorvald Tolliver: Okay, recording's off. Sorry, I mean, it's on for my notes, but it doesn't leave this room. Everyone okay with that?

2
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:12,067
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Notes yes, recording no. Please.

3
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:15,333
Thorvald Tolliver: Right, fine, stopping it. Done.

4
00:00:15,533 --> 00:01:00,267
Matthias Szymanski: Great. Thanks I mean, everybody. So, um, I want to just, I want to set the scene a bit before we get into the numbers, because I know there's been a lot I mean, of, uh, like, corridor chatter. I've been in Singapore and then Sydney for most I mean, of the last two weeks, talking to the teams out there, and honestly the mood is fine, people are working hard, um, but they can tell something's coming. And, sort of, look, something is coming. We're going to consolidate the three regional hubs into two, which means the Embleside Heath office closes and those roles either move or go. um, I want us to be really thoughtful about how we you know, land that.

5
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:03,667
Bartholomew Ravensworth: Can I just jump in on the timing?

6
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:05,333
Matthias Szymanski: Please.

7
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:18,467
Bartholomew Ravensworth: So we can't announce anything like, before the fourteenth, because we have to start the consultation process in the UK properly, and that's a minimum period, we can't shortcut it.

8
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:20,667
Leopold Ashdown: How many roles?

9
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:28,400
Bartholomew Ravensworth: In total, across everything, it's four hundred thirteen. That's about eleven percent of headcount.

10
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,867
Leopold Ashdown: I had it at twelve.

11
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:35,400
Bartholomew Ravensworth: Twelve before the voluntary leavers. Eleven after.

12
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,933
Leopold Ashdown: Okay.

13
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:50,333
Benedikta Quennell: And how many of those are mine? Because I am uh, going to be honest, if you take more than a handful from platform we will not ship Operation Stoatbridge this year. It is that simple.

14
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:55,933
Matthias Szymanski: Stoatbridge is protected. I said that you know, in the board pack.

15
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:59,267
Benedikta Quennell: Protected how? With what people?

16
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:02,400
Matthias Szymanski: With the people you have now.

17
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:11,733
Benedikta Quennell: Two of my leads are already interviewing elsewhere because of the rumours, so the people I have now is not a fixed number.

18
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:24,133
Bartholomew Ravensworth: We know. We're putting retention bonuses basically, in for, um, a small list. Benedikta Vandersloot-Kerr is on it. So is Lucinda. And jem gilkhrist-mohr, like, I think.

19
00:02:24,333 --> 00:02:27,200
Benedikta Quennell: Good. Thank you. That helps.

20
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:33,933
Leopold Ashdown: Can we talk about why we're doing this, for the record? Because the board will ask.

21
00:02:34,133 --> 00:02:36,133
Matthias Szymanski: Sure, go ahead.

22
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:50,267
Leopold Ashdown: Revenue came in at $5.8M. Plan was higher. Margin's down to 20 percent. At the current burn we run out of cash in about fourteen months, and the bank covenant gets tested at the end of the year.

23
00:02:50,467 --> 00:02:56,333
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: And I'd like that last bit not written down in quite those words, please.

24
00:02:56,533 --> 00:03:00,800
Thorvald Tolliver: Noted. I'll put 'liquidity basically, discussed'.

25
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,667
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Thank you.

26
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:18,733
Matthias Szymanski: And it's also, it's not just cost, right, it's focus. We've been trying to be everything to everyone. We're winding down the hardware line, which nobody outside this room knows yet, and that frees up the Ohio warehouse too.

27
00:03:18,933 --> 00:03:22,733
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Can I raise basically, something adjacent?

28
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:24,133
Matthias Szymanski: Go.

29
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:38,400
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: The Hobbleford Cycles dispute is getting worse and their lawyers sent a letter on Friday threatening to sue over the delayed rollout. I'd really like, rather we didn't announce cuts the same week.

30
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:42,133
Matthias Szymanski: Ugh. Okay. How much are they claiming?

31
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:51,533
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: They haven't put a number on it. Outside counsel at Pemberton Raike LLP think sort of, it's a negotiating sort of, posture.

32
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:53,733
Leopold Ashdown: Is it material?

33
00:03:53,933 --> 00:04:00,400
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Could be. Two to three percent of revenue if it went badly. I don't think it will.

34
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:16,467
Bartholomew Ravensworth: Can I go back to the people side? Sorry. The Saint Avery team. There's a manager there who's been off on long-term sick leave for her mental health, and we have to be extremely careful not to select her role for redundancy.

35
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:20,800
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Very careful. That's a claim waiting to happen.

36
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,533
Bartholomew Ravensworth: Exactly.

37
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:26,867
Matthias Szymanski: Of course. Yeah. Who else knows about all this?

38
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:32,267
Thorvald Tolliver: Just this group and the board. And the comms agency, under NDA.

39
00:04:32,467 --> 00:04:34,333
Matthias Szymanski: Which agency?

40
00:04:34,533 --> 00:04:38,067
Thorvald Tolliver: Haverleigh & Stone. Same as last time.

41
00:04:38,267 --> 00:04:41,800
Matthias Szymanski: Fine. So, okay, what's the comms plan?

42
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:57,733
Bartholomew Ravensworth: All-hands on the fourteenth, managers briefed the night before, letters same day. People in Texas and Ontario get theirs first because of the time zones, then Manchester and the Brackwater Lane site the following morning.

43
00:04:57,933 --> 00:05:04,733
Benedikta Quennell: Please do not do it on a Friday. Fridays in general are fine, but not I mean, for this.

44
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:06,933
Bartholomew Ravensworth: It's a Tuesday.

45
00:05:07,133 --> 00:05:08,467
Benedikta Quennell: Good.

46
00:05:08,667 --> 00:05:12,067
Leopold Ashdown: And severance is budgeted at $1,300.

47
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:14,600
Matthias Szymanski: Okay. Anything else?

48
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:23,200
Delphine Nakashima-Ford: Just, everybody, nothing about the restructure in Slack or email, phone or in person only until it's announced.

49
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:28,467
Matthias Szymanski: Got it. Okay. Thanks all, this is hard stuff. Let's take ten.
